# WebSocket Sec-WebSocket-Accept golden vectors (RFC 6455).
#
# The server computes:
#   accept = base64( SHA-1( key + "258EAFA5-E914-47DA-95CA-C5AB0DC85B11" ) )
# where `key` is the client's Sec-WebSocket-Key header value (a
# base64 string) and the GUID is the RFC 6455 magic constant.
#
# Format (fields '|'-separated):
#   <name> | <sec-websocket-key> | <expected-accept>
#
# The first row is the normative RFC 6455 §1.3 example — if this ever
# fails, the SHA-1 (NET-11.2) or base64 (NET-11.3) primitive is wrong.
rfc-example | dGhlIHNhbXBsZSBub25jZQ== | s3pPLMBiTxaQ9kYGzzhZRbK+xOo=
all-zeros   | AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA== | ICX+Yqv66kxgM0FcWaLWlFLwTAI=
